  "factor_name": "Risk-normalized shock reversal with trend persistence filter",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "CS_rank(-clip(sum(log_return,5)/(std(log_return,20)*sqrt(20)), -4, 4)) * CS_rank(clip(1-abs(sum(log_return,60)/sum(abs(log_return),60)), 0, 1)); lag(signal,1)",
    "description": "Ranks the negative five-day volatility-normalized move (favoring reversal after unusually large shocks), then multiplies by a cross-sectional rank of directional inefficiency over 60 days so persistent directional trends receive less reversal weight. The complete signal is lagged one session."
